#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM percuma tentang maklumat dan pengkomputeran kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formulations of measurements"
msgstr "Formulasi matematik pengukuran"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore biggr Biggr operatorname */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore biggr Biggr operatorname */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The lesson begins with two equivalent mathematical descriptions of measurements:\n"
msgstr "Pelajaran ini bermula dengan dua huraian matematik yang setara bagi pengukuran:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "General measurements can be described by *collections of matrices*, one for each measurement outcome, in a way that generalizes the description of projective measurements.\n"
msgstr "Pengukuran umum boleh dihuraikan oleh *koleksi matriks*, satu bagi setiap hasil pengukuran, dengan cara yang mengeneralisasikan huraian pengukuran unjuran.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "General measurements can be described as *channels* whose outputs are always classical states (represented by diagonal density matrices).\n"
msgstr "Pengukuran umum boleh dihuraikan sebagai *saluran* yang outputnya sentiasa merupakan keadaan klasik (diwakili oleh matriks ketumpatan pepenjuru).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll restrict our attention to measurements having *finitely many* possible outcomes.\n"
"Although it is possible to define measurements with infinitely many possible outcomes, they're much less typically encountered in the context of computation and information processing, and they also require some additional mathematics (namely measure theory) to be properly formalized.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan menumpukan perhatian pada pengukuran yang mempunyai *bilangan hasil yang terhingga*.\n"
"Walaupun pengukuran dengan hasil tidak terhingga boleh ditakrifkan, ia jarang ditemui dalam konteks pengkomputeran dan pemprosesan maklumat, dan ia juga memerlukan matematik tambahan (iaitu teori ukur) untuk diformalisasikan dengan betul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our initial focus will be on so-called *destructive* measurements, where the output of the measurement is a classical measurement outcome alone — with no specification of the post-measurement quantum state of whatever system was measured.\n"
"Intuitively speaking, we can imagine that such a measurement destroys the quantum system itself, or that the system is immediately discarded once the measurement is made.\n"
"Later in the lesson we'll broaden our view and consider *non-destructive* measurements, where there's both a classical measurement outcome and a post-measurement quantum state of the measured system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fokus awal kita adalah pada pengukuran yang dikenali sebagai pengukuran *merosakkan*, di mana output pengukuran hanyalah hasil pengukuran klasik semata-mata — tanpa spesifikasi keadaan kuantum pasca-pengukuran sistem yang diukur.\n"
"Secara intuitif, kita boleh bayangkan bahawa pengukuran sedemikian memusnahkan sistem kuantum itu sendiri, atau bahawa sistem itu segera dibuang setelah pengukuran dibuat.\n"
"Kemudian dalam pelajaran ini kita akan meluaskan pandangan dan mempertimbangkan pengukuran *tidak merosakkan*, di mana terdapat kedua-dua hasil pengukuran klasik dan keadaan kuantum pasca-pengukuran sistem yang diukur.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measurements as collections of matrices {#measurements-as-collections-of-matrices}"
msgstr "Pengukuran sebagai koleksi matriks {#measurements-as-collections-of-matrices}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system that is to be measured, and assume for simplicity that the classical state set of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\{0,\\ldots, n-1\\}$ for some positive integer $n$, so that density matrices representing quantum states of $\\mathsf{X}$ are $n\\times n$ matrices.\n"
"We won't actually have much need to refer to the classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$, but it will be convenient to refer to $n$, the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"We'll also assume that the possible outcomes of the measurement are the integers $0,\\ldots,m-1$ for some positive integer $m$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Andaikan $\\mathsf{X}$ ialah sistem yang hendak diukur, dan andaikan untuk kesederhanaan bahawa set keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$ ialah $\\{0,\\ldots, n-1\\}$ bagi suatu integer positif $n$, supaya matriks ketumpatan yang mewakili keadaan kuantum $\\mathsf{X}$ ialah matriks $n\\times n$.\n"
"Sebenarnya kita tidak banyak perlu merujuk kepada keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$, tetapi akan lebih mudah untuk merujuk kepada $n$, iaitu bilangan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Kita juga akan menganggap hasil-hasil pengukuran yang mungkin ialah integer $0,\\ldots,m-1$ bagi suatu integer positif $m$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that we're just using these names to keep things simple;\n"
"it's straightforward to generalize everything that follows to other finite sets of classical states and measurement outcomes, renaming them as desired.\n"
msgstr "Perlu diingat bahawa kita hanya menggunakan nama-nama ini untuk memudahkan perkara; adalah mudah untuk mengeneralisasikan semua yang berikut kepada set terhingga keadaan klasik dan hasil pengukuran lain, dengan menamakan semula seperti yang diingini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projective measurements {#projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Pengukuran unjuran {#projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that a *projective measurement* is described by a collection of *projection matrices* that sum to the identity matrix.\n"
"In symbols,\n"
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahawa *pengukuran unjuran* dihuraikan oleh koleksi *matriks unjuran* yang berjumlah kepada matriks identiti.\n"
"Dalam simbol,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "describes a projective measurement of $\\mathsf{X}$ if each $\\Pi_a$ is an $n\\times n$ projection matrix and the following condition is met.\n"
msgstr "menghuraikan pengukuran unjuran $\\mathsf{X}$ jika setiap $\\Pi_a$ ialah matriks unjuran $n\\times n$ dan syarat berikut dipenuhi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When such a measurement is performed on a system $\\mathsf{X}$ while it's in a state described by some quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, each outcome $a$ is obtained with probability equal to $\\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2$.\n"
"We also have that the post-measurement state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is obtained by normalizing the vector $\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, but we're ignoring the post-measurement state for now.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila pengukuran sedemikian dilakukan pada sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ semasa ia berada dalam keadaan yang dihuraikan oleh suatu vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, setiap hasil $a$ diperoleh dengan kebarangkalian sama dengan $\\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2$.\n"
"Kita juga mempunyai bahawa keadaan pasca-pengukuran $\\mathsf{X}$ diperoleh dengan menormalkan vektor $\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, tetapi kita mengabaikan keadaan pasca-pengukuran buat masa ini.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is described by a density matrix $\\rho$ rather than a quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, then we can alternatively express the probability to obtain the outcome $a$ as $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr "Jika keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ dihuraikan oleh matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ dan bukannya vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, maka kita boleh secara alternatif menyatakan kebarangkalian untuk memperoleh hasil $a$ sebagai $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $\\rho = \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ is a pure state, then the two expressions are equal:\n"
msgstr "Jika $\\rho = \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ ialah keadaan tulen, maka kedua-dua ungkapan adalah sama:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi \\vert)\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi \\vert)\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we're using the cyclic property of the trace for the second equality, and for the third equality we're using the fact that each $\\Pi_a$ is a projection matrix, and therefore satisfies $\\Pi_a^2 = \\Pi_a$.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita menggunakan sifat siklik surih untuk persamaan kedua, dan untuk persamaan ketiga kita menggunakan fakta bahawa setiap $\\Pi_a$ ialah matriks unjuran, dan oleh itu memenuhi $\\Pi_a^2 = \\Pi_a$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In general, if $\\rho$ is a convex combination\n"
msgstr "Secara umum, jika $\\rho$ ialah kombinasi cembung\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "of pure states, then the expression $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$ coincides with the average probability for the outcome $a$, owing to the fact that this expression is linear in $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr "bagi keadaan-keadaan tulen, maka ungkapan $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$ berpadanan dengan kebarangkalian purata untuk hasil $a$, disebabkan fakta bahawa ungkapan ini adalah linear dalam $\\rho$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\|^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\|^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "General measurements {#general-measurements}"
msgstr "Pengukuran umum {#general-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A mathematical description for general measurements is obtained by relaxing the definition of projective measurements.\n"
"Specifically, we allow the matrices in the collection describing the measurement to be arbitrary *positive semidefinite* matrices rather than projections.\n"
"(Projections are always positive semidefinite; they can alternatively be defined as positive semidefinite matrices whose eigenvalues are all either 0 or 1.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Huraian matematik bagi pengukuran umum diperoleh dengan melonggarkan takrifan pengukuran unjuran.\n"
"Secara khusus, kita membenarkan matriks dalam koleksi yang menghuraikan pengukuran menjadi matriks *separuh-tentu positif* yang sewenang-wenangnya dan bukannya unjuran.\n"
"(Unjuran sentiasa separuh-tentu positif; ia boleh ditakrifkan secara alternatif sebagai matriks separuh-tentu positif yang nilai eigennya semuanya sama ada 0 atau 1.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, a general measurement of a system $\\mathsf{X}$ having outcomes $0,\\ldots,m-1$ is specified by a collection of positive semidefinite matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ whose rows and columns correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and that meet the condition\n"
msgstr "Khususnya, pengukuran umum bagi sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ yang mempunyai hasil $0,\\ldots,m-1$ ditentukan oleh koleksi matriks separuh-tentu positif $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ yang baris dan lajurnya sepadan dengan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$ dan memenuhi syarat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is measured while it is in a state described by the density matrix $\\rho$, then each outcome\n"
"$a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ appears with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ diukur semasa ia berada dalam keadaan yang dihuraikan oleh matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$, maka setiap hasil\n"
"$a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ muncul dengan kebarangkalian $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As we must naturally demand, the vector of outcome probabilities\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang semestinya kita tuntut, vektor kebarangkalian hasil\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho),\\ldots,\\operatorname{Tr}(P_{m-1} \\rho)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho),\\ldots,\\operatorname{Tr}(P_{m-1} \\rho)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"of a general measurement always forms a probability vector, for any choice of a density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
"The following two observations establish that this is the case.\n"
msgstr ""
"bagi pengukuran umum sentiasa membentuk vektor kebarangkalian, bagi mana-mana pilihan matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$.\n"
"Dua pemerhatian berikut menetapkan bahawa ini memang kes demikian.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each value $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$ must be nonnegative, owing to the fact that the trace of the product of any two positive semidefinite matrices is always nonnegative:\n"
msgstr "Setiap nilai $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$ mestilah bukan negatif, disebabkan fakta bahawa surih darab mana-mana dua matriks separuh-tentu positif sentiasa bukan negatif:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   Q, R \\geq 0 \\; \\Rightarrow \\: \\operatorname{Tr}(QR) \\geq 0.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   Q, R \\geq 0 \\; \\Rightarrow \\: \\operatorname{Tr}(QR) \\geq 0.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   One way to argue this fact is to use spectral decompositions of $Q$ and $R$ together with the cyclic property of the trace to express the trace of the product $QR$ as a sum of nonnegative real numbers, which must therefore be nonnegative.\n"
msgstr "   Satu cara untuk membuktikan fakta ini ialah menggunakan penguraian spektrum $Q$ dan $R$ bersama-sama dengan sifat siklik surih untuk menyatakan surih darab $QR$ sebagai jumlah nombor nyata bukan negatif, yang oleh itu mestilah bukan negatif.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The condition $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ together with the linearity of the trace ensures that the probabilities sum to $1$.\n"
msgstr "Syarat $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ bersama-sama dengan lineariti surih memastikan bahawa kebarangkalian-kebarangkalian berjumlah kepada $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}\\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a \\rho\\Biggr)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\mathbb{I}\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) = 1\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}\\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a \\rho\\Biggr)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\mathbb{I}\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) = 1\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 1: any projective measurement {#example-1-any-projective-measurement}"
msgstr "Contoh 1: mana-mana pengukuran unjuran {#example-1-any-projective-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projections are always positive semidefinite, so every projective measurement is an example of a general measurement.\n"
msgstr "Unjuran sentiasa separuh-tentu positif, jadi setiap pengukuran unjuran adalah contoh pengukuran umum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, a standard basis measurement of a qubit can be represented by $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ where\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, pengukuran asas piawai qubit boleh diwakili oleh $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ di mana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"P_1 = \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{dan}\\quad\n"
"P_1 = \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring a qubit in the state $\\rho$ results in outcome probabilities as follows.\n"
msgstr "Mengukur qubit dalam keadaan $\\rho$ menghasilkan kebarangkalian hasil seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 0)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 0\\vert \\rho \\vert 0 \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 1)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 1 \\vert \\rho \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{hasil} = 0)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 0\\vert \\rho \\vert 0 \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{hasil} = 1)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 1 \\vert \\rho \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 2: a non-projective qubit measurement {#example-2-a-non-projective-qubit-measurement}"
msgstr "Contoh 2: pengukuran qubit bukan unjuran {#example-2-a-non-projective-qubit-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a qubit, and define two matrices as follows.\n"
msgstr "Andaikan $\\mathsf{X}$ ialah qubit, dan takrifkan dua matriks seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"P_1 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"P_1 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These are both positive semidefinite matrices: they're Hermitian, and in both cases the eigenvalues happen to be $1/2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}/6$, which are both positive.\n"
"We also have that $P_0 + P_1 = \\mathbb{I}$, and therefore $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ describes a measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua-duanya adalah matriks separuh-tentu positif: ia adalah Hermitian, dan dalam kedua-dua kes nilai eigen kebetulan ialah $1/2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}/6$, yang kedua-duanya positif.\n"
"Kita juga mempunyai bahawa $P_0 + P_1 = \\mathbb{I}$, dan oleh itu $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ menghuraikan sebuah pengukuran.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is described by a density matrix $\\rho$ and we perform this measurement, then the probability of obtaining the outcome $0$ is $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)$ and the probability of obtaining the outcome $1$ is\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)$.\n"
"For instance, if $\\rho = \\vert + \\rangle \\langle + \\vert$ then the probabilities for the two outcomes $0$ and $1$ are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ dihuraikan oleh matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ dan kita melakukan pengukuran ini, maka kebarangkalian mendapat hasil $0$ ialah $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)$ dan kebarangkalian mendapat hasil $1$ ialah\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)$.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, jika $\\rho = \\vert + \\rangle \\langle + \\vert$ maka kebarangkalian bagi kedua-dua hasil $0$ dan $1$ adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{6}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = 0 + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{6}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{6}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = 0 + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{6}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 3: tetrahedral measurement {#example-3-tetrahedral-measurement}"
msgstr "Contoh 3: pengukuran tetrahedron {#example-3-tetrahedral-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define four single-qubit quantum state vectors as follows.\n"
msgstr "Takrifkan empat vektor keadaan kuantum qubit tunggal seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle & = \\vert 0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_2\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_3\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{-2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle & = \\vert 0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_2\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_3\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{-2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These four states are sometimes known as *tetrahedral* states because they're vertices of a *regular tetrahedron* inscribed within the Bloch sphere.\n"
msgstr "Keempat-empat keadaan ini kadang-kadang dikenali sebagai keadaan *tetrahedron* kerana ia adalah bucu-bucu sebuah *tetrahedron sekata* yang tertulis dalam sfera Bloch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Illustration of a tetrahedron inscribed in the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/general-measurements/tetrahedral-states.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Ilustrasi tetrahedron yang tertulis dalam sfera Bloch](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/general-measurements/tetrahedral-states.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Cartesian coordinates of these four states on the Bloch sphere are\n"
msgstr "Koordinat Cartesian keempat-empat keadaan ini pada sfera Bloch ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(0,0,1),\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\left( \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} , 0 , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , -\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(0,0,1),\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\left( \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} , 0 , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , -\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which can be verified by expressing the density matrices representations of these states as linear combinations of Pauli matrices.\n"
msgstr "yang boleh disahkan dengan menyatakan perwakilan matriks ketumpatan keadaan-keadaan ini sebagai kombinasi linear matriks Pauli.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_0 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_0 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_0 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_0 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_1 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_1 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_2 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_2 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_3 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_3 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_3 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_3 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These four states are perfectly spread out on the Bloch sphere, each one equidistant from the other three and with the angles between any two of them always being the same.\n"
msgstr "Keempat-empat keadaan ini tersebar dengan sempurna di atas sfera Bloch, masing-masing sama jauh dari tiga yang lain dan dengan sudut antara mana-mana dua daripadanya sentiasa sama.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let us define a measurement $\\{P_0,P_1,P_2,P_3\\}$ of a qubit by setting $P_a$ as follows for each $a=0,\\ldots,3$.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang mari kita takrifkan pengukuran $\\{P_0,P_1,P_2,P_3\\}$ bagi qubit dengan menetapkan $P_a$ seperti berikut bagi setiap $a=0,\\ldots,3$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\frac{\\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\frac{\\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can verify that this is a valid measurement as follows.\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh mengesahkan bahawa ini adalah pengukuran yang sah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each $P_a$ is evidently positive semidefinite, being a pure state divided by one-half.\n"
"That is, each one is a Hermitian matrix and has one eigenvalue equal to $1/2$ and all other eigenvalues zero.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap $P_a$ jelas separuh-tentu positif, kerana ia adalah keadaan tulen dibahagi dengan satu per dua.\n"
"Yakni, setiap satunya ialah matriks Hermitian yang mempunyai satu nilai eigen sama dengan $1/2$ dan semua nilai eigen lain sifar.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The sum of these matrices is the identity matrix: $P_0 + P_1 + P_2 + P_3 = \\mathbb{I}$.\n"
"The expressions of these matrices as linear combinations of Pauli matrices makes this straightforward to verify.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jumlah matriks-matriks ini ialah matriks identiti: $P_0 + P_1 + P_2 + P_3 = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
"Ungkapan matriks-matriks ini sebagai kombinasi linear matriks Pauli menjadikan ini mudah untuk disahkan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measurements as channels {#measurements-as-channels}"
msgstr "Pengukuran sebagai saluran {#measurements-as-channels}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A second way to describe measurements in mathematical terms is as channels.\n"
msgstr "Cara kedua untuk menerangkan pengukuran dalam istilah matematik ialah sebagai saluran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Classical information can be viewed as a special case of quantum information, insofar as we can identify probabilistic states with diagonal density matrices.\n"
"So, in operational terms, we can think about measurements as being channels whose inputs are matrices describing states of whatever system is being measured and whose outputs are *diagonal* density matrices describing the resulting distribution of measurement outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maklumat klasik boleh dilihat sebagai kes khas maklumat kuantum, setakat mana kita boleh mengenal pasti keadaan probabilistik dengan matriks ketumpatan pepenjuru.\n"
"Jadi, dalam istilah operasi, kita boleh memikirkan pengukuran sebagai saluran yang inputnya ialah matriks yang menerangkan keadaan sistem yang diukur dan outputnya ialah matriks ketumpatan *pepenjuru* yang menerangkan taburan hasil pengukuran yang terhasil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll see shortly that any channel having this property can always be written in a simple, canonical form that ties directly to the description of measurements as collections of positive semidefinite matrices.\n"
"Conversely, given an arbitrary measurement as a collection of matrices, there's always a valid channel having the diagonal output property that describes the given measurement as suggested in the previous paragraph.\n"
"Putting these observations together, we find that the two descriptions of general measurements are equivalent.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan lihat tidak lama lagi bahawa sebarang saluran yang mempunyai sifat ini sentiasa boleh ditulis dalam bentuk kanonik yang mudah dan berkaitan terus dengan penerangan pengukuran sebagai koleksi matriks semidefinit positif.\n"
"Sebaliknya, diberi pengukuran umum sebagai koleksi matriks, sentiasa ada saluran sah yang mempunyai sifat output pepenjuru yang menerangkan pengukuran yang diberi seperti yang dicadangkan dalam perenggan sebelumnya.\n"
"Dengan menggabungkan pemerhatian-pemerhatian ini, kita dapati bahawa dua penerangan pengukuran umum adalah setara.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before proceeding further, let's be more precise about the measurement, how we're viewing it as a channel, and what assumptions we're making about it.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum meneruskan lebih jauh, mari kita lebih tepat mengenai pengukuran, bagaimana kita memandangnya sebagai saluran, dan andaian-andaian yang kita buat.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As before, we'll suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ is the system to be measured, and that the possible outcomes of the measurement are the integers $0,\\ldots,m-1$ for some positive integer $m$.\n"
"We let $\\mathsf{Y}$ be the system that stores measurement outcomes, so its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, and we represent the measurement as a channel named $\\Phi$ from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Our assumption is that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is *classical* — which is to say that no matter what state we start with for $\\mathsf{X}$, the state of $\\mathsf{Y}$ we obtain is represented by a diagonal density matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti sebelumnya, kita andaikan $\\mathsf{X}$ ialah sistem yang hendak diukur, dan kemungkinan hasil pengukuran ialah integer $0,\\ldots,m-1$ untuk sesetengah integer positif $m$.\n"
"Kita biarkan $\\mathsf{Y}$ menjadi sistem yang menyimpan hasil pengukuran, jadi set keadaan klasiknya ialah $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, dan kita wakilkan pengukuran sebagai saluran bernama $\\Phi$ dari $\\mathsf{X}$ ke $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Andaian kita ialah $\\mathsf{Y}$ bersifat *klasik* — bermakna tidak kira apa keadaan awal $\\mathsf{X}$, keadaan $\\mathsf{Y}$ yang kita peroleh sentiasa diwakili oleh matriks ketumpatan pepenjuru.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can express in mathematical terms that the output of $\\Phi$ is always diagonal in the following way.\n"
"First define the completely dephasing channel $\\Delta_m$ on $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh nyatakan dalam istilah matematik bahawa output $\\Phi$ sentiasa pepenjuru dengan cara berikut.\n"
"Mula-mula takrifkan saluran penyahfasa penuh $\\Delta_m$ pada $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta_m(\\sigma) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\sigma \\vert a\\rangle \\,\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta_m(\\sigma) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\sigma \\vert a\\rangle \\,\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This channel is analogous to the completely dephasing qubit channel $\\Delta$ from the previous lesson.\n"
"As a linear mapping, it zeros out all of the off-diagonal entries of an input matrix and leaves the diagonal alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Saluran ini analog dengan saluran penyahfasa penuh qubit $\\Delta$ dari pelajaran sebelumnya.\n"
"Sebagai pemetaan linear, ia menghapuskan semua entri luar pepenjuru matriks input dan membiarkan pepenjuru tidak berubah.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now, a simple way to express that a given density matrix $\\sigma$ is diagonal is by the equation\n"
"$\\sigma = \\Delta_m(\\sigma)$.\n"
"In words, zeroing out all of the off-diagonal entries of a density matrix has no effect if and only if the off-diagonal entries were all zero to begin with.\n"
"The channel $\\Phi$ therefore satisfies our assumption — that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is classical — if and only if\n"
msgstr ""
"Kini, cara mudah untuk menyatakan bahawa matriks ketumpatan $\\sigma$ tertentu adalah pepenjuru ialah melalui persamaan\n"
"$\\sigma = \\Delta_m(\\sigma)$.\n"
"Dengan kata lain, menghapuskan semua entri luar pepenjuru matriks ketumpatan tidak memberi kesan jika dan hanya jika entri luar pepenjuru tersebut sudah sifar dari awal.\n"
"Saluran $\\Phi$ oleh itu memenuhi andaian kita — bahawa $\\mathsf{Y}$ bersifat klasik — jika dan hanya jika\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\Delta_m(\\Phi(\\rho))\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\Delta_m(\\Phi(\\rho))\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for every density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr "untuk setiap matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ yang mewakili keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Equivalence of the formulations {#equivalence-of-the-formulations}"
msgstr "Kesetaraan formulasi {#equivalence-of-the-formulations}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Channels to matrices {#channels-to-matrices}"
msgstr "Saluran kepada matriks {#channels-to-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose that we have a channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$ with the property that\n"
msgstr "Andaikan kita mempunyai saluran dari $\\mathsf{X}$ ke $\\mathsf{Y}$ dengan sifat bahawa\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for every density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
"This may alternatively be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk setiap matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$.\n"
"Ini boleh dinyatakan secara alternatif seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Like all channels, we can express $\\Phi$ in Kraus form for some way of choosing Kraus matrices\n"
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti semua saluran, kita boleh nyatakan $\\Phi$ dalam bentuk Kraus untuk sesetengah cara memilih matriks Kraus\n"
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This provides us with an alternative expression for the diagonal entries of $\\Phi(\\rho)\\!:$\n"
msgstr "Ini memberi kita ungkapan alternatif untuk entri pepenjuru $\\Phi(\\rho)\\!:$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(P_a\\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(P_a\\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "untuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, for these same matrices $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ we can express the channel $\\Phi$ as follows.\n"
msgstr "Oleh itu, untuk matriks $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ yang sama ini, kita boleh nyatakan saluran $\\Phi$ seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This expression is consistent with our description of general measurements in terms of matrices, as we see each measurement outcome appearing with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr "Ungkapan ini konsisten dengan penerangan kita tentang pengukuran umum dalam bentuk matriks, di mana kita lihat setiap hasil pengukuran muncul dengan kebarangkalian $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's observe that the two properties required of the collection of matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ to describe a general measurement are indeed satisfied.\n"
"The first property is that they're all positive semidefinite matrices.\n"
"One way to see this is to observe that, for every vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ having entries in correspondence with the classical state of $\\mathsf{X}$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita perhatikan bahawa dua sifat yang diperlukan koleksi matriks $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ untuk menerangkan pengukuran umum memang dipenuhi.\n"
"Sifat pertama ialah ia semua adalah matriks semidefinit positif.\n"
"Salah satu cara untuk melihat ini ialah dengan memerhatikan bahawa, untuk setiap vektor $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ yang entrinya berpadanan dengan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$ kita ada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert P_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle \\psi \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"=  \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\bigl\\vert\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\vert^2 \\geq 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert P_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle \\psi \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"=  \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\bigl\\vert\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\vert^2 \\geq 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second property is that if we sum these matrices we get the identity matrix.\n"
msgstr "Sifat kedua ialah jika kita jumlahkan matriks-matriks ini kita mendapat matriks identiti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\Biggr) A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\Biggr) A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last equality follows from the fact that $\\Phi$ is a channel, so its Kraus matrices must satisfy this condition.\n"
msgstr "Kesamaan terakhir mengikut dari fakta bahawa $\\Phi$ ialah saluran, jadi matriks Krausnya mesti memenuhi syarat ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrices to channels {#matrices-to-channels}"
msgstr "Matriks kepada saluran {#matrices-to-channels}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's verify that for any collection $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ of positive semidefinite matrices satisfying $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$, the mapping defined by\n"
msgstr "Sekarang mari kita sahkan bahawa untuk sebarang koleksi $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ matriks semidefinit positif yang memenuhi $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$, pemetaan yang ditakrifkan oleh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is indeed a valid channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
msgstr "memang merupakan saluran sah dari $\\mathsf{X}$ ke $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One way to do this is to compute the Choi representation of this mapping.\n"
msgstr "Salah satu cara untuk melakukan ini ialah dengan mengira perwakilan Choi bagi pemetaan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Phi) & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes \\Phi(\\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Phi) & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes \\Phi(\\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The transpose of each $P_a$ is introduced for the third equality because\n"
msgstr "Transpose setiap $P_a$ diperkenalkan untuk kesamaan ketiga kerana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle c \\vert P_a \\vert b\\rangle = \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle c \\vert P_a \\vert b\\rangle = \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This allows for the expressions $\\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert$ and $\\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert$ to appear, which simplify to the identity matrix upon summing over $b$ and $c$, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Ini membolehkan ungkapan $\\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert$ dan $\\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert$ muncul, yang menjadi matriks identiti apabila dijumlahkan ke atas $b$ dan $c$ masing-masing.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the assumption that $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ are positive semidefinite, so too are $P_0^{T},\\ldots,P_{m-1}^{T}$.\n"
"In particular, transposing a Hermitian matrix results in another Hermitian matrix, and the eigenvalues of any square matrix and its transpose always agree.\n"
"It follows that $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite.\n"
"Tracing out the output system $\\mathsf{Y}$ (which is the system on the right) yields\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan andaian bahawa $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ adalah semidefinit positif, begitu juga $P_0^{T},\\ldots,P_{m-1}^{T}$.\n"
"Khususnya, mentranspos matriks Hermitian menghasilkan matriks Hermitian yang lain, dan nilai eigen sebarang matriks persegi dan transposenya sentiasa sama.\n"
"Oleh itu $J(\\Phi)$ adalah semidefinit positif.\n"
"Mensurih keluar sistem output $\\mathsf{Y}$ (iaitu sistem di sebelah kanan) menghasilkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and so we conclude that $\\Phi$ is a channel.\n"
msgstr "jadi kita simpulkan bahawa $\\Phi$ ialah saluran.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial measurements {#partial-measurements}"
msgstr "Pengukuran separa {#partial-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have multiple systems that are collectively in a quantum state, and a general measurement is performed on one of the systems.\n"
"This results in one of the measurement outcomes, selected at random according to probabilities determined by the measurement and the state of the system prior to the measurement.\n"
"The resulting state of the remaining systems will then, in general, depend on which measurement outcome was obtained.\n"
msgstr ""
"Andaikan kita mempunyai berbilang sistem yang bersama-sama berada dalam keadaan kuantum, dan pengukuran umum dilakukan pada salah satu sistem.\n"
"Ini menghasilkan salah satu hasil pengukuran, dipilih secara rawak mengikut kebarangkalian yang ditentukan oleh pengukuran dan keadaan sistem sebelum pengukuran.\n"
"Keadaan sistem yang tinggal kemudiannya, secara umum, bergantung pada hasil pengukuran yang diperoleh.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's examine how this works for a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ when the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is measured.\n"
"(We're naming the system on the right $\\mathsf{Z}$ because we'll take $\\mathsf{Y}$ to be a system representing the classical output of the measurement when we view it as a channel.)\n"
"We can then easily generalize to the situation in which the systems are swapped as well as to three or more systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita kaji bagaimana ini berlaku untuk pasangan sistem $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ apabila sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ diukur.\n"
"(Kita namakan sistem di sebelah kanan $\\mathsf{Z}$ kerana kita akan gunakan $\\mathsf{Y}$ sebagai sistem yang mewakili output klasik pengukuran apabila kita melihatnya sebagai saluran.)\n"
"Kita kemudiannya boleh generalisasikan dengan mudah kepada situasi di mana urutan sistem diterbalikkan serta kepada tiga sistem atau lebih.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ prior to the measurement is described by a density matrix $\\rho$, which we can write as follows.\n"
msgstr "Andaikan keadaan $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ sebelum pengukuran diterangkan oleh matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$, yang boleh kita tulis seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this expression we're assuming the classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ are $0,\\ldots,n-1$.\n"
msgstr "Dalam ungkapan ini kita andaikan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$ ialah $0,\\ldots,n-1$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll assume that the measurement itself is described by the collection of matrices\n"
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$.\n"
"This measurement may alternatively be described as a channel $\\Phi$ from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$, where $\\mathsf{Y}$ is a new system having classical state set $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"
"Specifically, the action of this channel can be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita andaikan pengukuran itu sendiri diterangkan oleh koleksi matriks\n"
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$.\n"
"Pengukuran ini boleh diterangkan secara alternatif sebagai saluran $\\Phi$ dari $\\mathsf{X}$ ke $\\mathsf{Y}$, di mana $\\mathsf{Y}$ ialah sistem baru yang mempunyai set keadaan klasik $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"
"Khususnya, tindakan saluran ini boleh dinyatakan seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\xi) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\xi)\\, \\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\xi) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\xi)\\, \\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Outcome probabilities {#outcome-probabilities}"
msgstr "Kebarangkalian hasil pengukuran {#outcome-probabilities}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We're considering a measurement of the system $\\mathsf{X}$, so the probabilities with which different measurement outcomes are obtained can depend only on $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}$, the reduced state of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"In particular, the probability for each outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ to appear can be expressed in three equivalent ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sedang mempertimbangkan pengukuran sistem $\\mathsf{X}$, jadi kebarangkalian dengan mana hasil pengukuran yang berbeza diperoleh hanya boleh bergantung pada $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}$, keadaan terturun $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Khususnya, kebarangkalian untuk setiap hasil $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ muncul boleh dinyatakan dalam tiga cara yang setara.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( (P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( (P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first expression naturally represents the probability to obtain the outcome $a$ based on what we already know about measurements of a single system.\n"
"To get the second expression we're simply using the definition $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ungkapan pertama secara semula jadi mewakili kebarangkalian untuk memperoleh hasil $a$ berdasarkan apa yang kita sudah tahu tentang pengukuran sistem tunggal.\n"
"Untuk mendapatkan ungkapan kedua kita hanya menggunakan takrifan $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To get the third expression requires more thought — and learners are encouraged to convince themselves that it is true.\n"
"Here's a hint: The equivalence between the second and third expressions does not depend on $\\rho$ being a density matrix or on each $P_a$ being positive semidefinite. Try showing it first for tensor products of the form $\\rho = M\\otimes N$ and then conclude that it must be true in general by linearity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mendapatkan ungkapan ketiga memerlukan lebih banyak pemikiran — dan pelajar digalakkan untuk meyakinkan diri bahawa ia adalah benar.\n"
"Berikut adalah petunjuk: Kesetaraan antara ungkapan kedua dan ketiga dalam persamaan sebelumnya tidak bergantung pada $\\rho$ sebagai matriks ketumpatan atau pada setiap $P_a$ sebagai semidefinit positif. Cuba buktikan ia terlebih dahulu untuk hasil darab tensor berbentuk $\\rho = M\\otimes N$ dan kemudian simpulkan ia mesti benar secara umum melalui kelinearan.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the equivalence of the first and third expressions in the previous equation may not be immediate, it does make sense.\n"
"Starting from a measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$, we're effectively defining a measurement of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$, where we simply throw away $\\mathsf{Z}$ and measure $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Like all measurements, this new measurement can be described by a collection of matrices, and it's not surprising that this measurement is described by the collection\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun kesetaraan ungkapan pertama dan ketiga dalam persamaan sebelumnya mungkin tidak segera jelas, ia masuk akal.\n"
"Bermula dari pengukuran pada $\\mathsf{X}$, kita secara efektif mentakrifkan pengukuran $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$, di mana kita hanya membuang $\\mathsf{Z}$ dan mengukur $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Seperti semua pengukuran, pengukuran baru ini boleh diterangkan oleh koleksi matriks, dan tidak hairanlah pengukuran ini diterangkan oleh koleksi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{P_0\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}, \\ldots, P_{m-1}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{P_0\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}, \\ldots, P_{m-1}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "States conditioned on measurement outcomes {#states-conditioned-on-measurement-outcomes}"
msgstr "Keadaan bersyarat pada hasil pengukuran {#states-conditioned-on-measurement-outcomes}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we want to determine not only the probabilities for the different outcomes but also the resulting state of $\\mathsf{Z}$ conditioned on each measurement outcome, we can look to the channel description of the measurement.\n"
"In particular, let's examine the state we get when we apply $\\Phi$ to $\\mathsf{X}$ and do nothing to $\\mathsf{Z}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kita ingin menentukan bukan sahaja kebarangkalian untuk hasil yang berbeza tetapi juga keadaan $\\mathsf{Z}$ yang terhasil bersyarat pada setiap hasil pengukuran, kita boleh melihat kepada penerangan saluran bagi pengukuran tersebut.\n"
"Khususnya, mari kita kaji keadaan yang kita peroleh apabila kita menerapkan $\\Phi$ pada $\\mathsf{X}$ dan tidak melakukan apa-apa pada $\\mathsf{Z}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  (\\Phi\\otimes\\operatorname{Id}_{\\mathsf{Z}})(\\rho)\n"
"  & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\Phi(\\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert)\n"
"    \\,\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1}\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}})\n"
"    (\\vert b\\rangle\\langle  c\\vert\\otimes\\rho_{b,c})\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  (\\Phi\\otimes\\operatorname{Id}_{\\mathsf{Z}})(\\rho)\n"
"  & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\Phi(\\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert)\n"
"    \\,\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1}\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}})\n"
"    (\\vert b\\rangle\\langle  c\\vert\\otimes\\rho_{b,c})\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that this is a density matrix by virtue of the fact that $\\Phi$ is a channel, so each matrix\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$ is necessarily positive semidefinite.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa ini ialah matriks ketumpatan kerana $\\Phi$ ialah saluran, jadi setiap matriks\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$ semestinya semidefinit positif.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One final step transforms this expression into one that reveals what we're looking for.\n"
msgstr "Satu langkah terakhir mengubah ungkapan ini kepada satu yang mendedahkan apa yang kita cari.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is an example of a *classical-quantum state*,\n"
msgstr "Ini adalah contoh *keadaan klasik-kuantum*,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} p(a)\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert \\otimes \\sigma_a,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} p(a)\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert \\otimes \\sigma_a,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"like we saw in the *Density matrices* lesson.\n"
"For each measurement outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, we have with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"seperti yang kita lihat dalam pelajaran *Matriks ketumpatan*.\n"
"Untuk setiap hasil pengukuran $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, kita ada dengan kebarangkalian\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is in the classical state $\\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert$ and $\\mathsf{Z}$ is in the state\n"
msgstr "bahawa $\\mathsf{Y}$ berada dalam keadaan klasik $\\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert$ dan $\\mathsf{Z}$ berada dalam keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_a = \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_a = \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, this is the density matrix we obtain by normalizing\n"
msgstr "Iaitu, ini ialah matriks ketumpatan yang kita peroleh dengan menormalkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"by dividing it by its trace.\n"
"(Formally speaking, the state $\\sigma_a$ is only defined when the probability $p(a)$ is nonzero;\n"
"when $p(a) = 0$ this state is irrelevant, for it refers to a discrete event that occurs with probability zero.)\n"
msgstr ""
"dengan membahaginya dengan surihnya.\n"
"(Secara formal, keadaan $\\sigma_a$ hanya ditakrifkan apabila kebarangkalian $p(a)$ adalah bukan sifar;\n"
"apabila $p(a) = 0$ keadaan ini tidak relevan, kerana ia merujuk kepada peristiwa diskret yang berlaku dengan kebarangkalian sifar.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Naturally, the outcome probabilities are consistent with our previous observations.\n"
msgstr "Secara semula jadi, kebarangkalian hasil pengukuran adalah konsisten dengan pemerhatian kita sebelum ini.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In summary, this is what happens when the measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ is performed on $\\mathsf{X}$ when $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ is in the state $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr "Ringkasnya, inilah yang berlaku apabila pengukuran $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ dilakukan pada $\\mathsf{X}$ apabila $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ berada dalam keadaan $\\rho$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each outcome $a$ appears with probability $p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr "Setiap hasil $a$ muncul dengan kebarangkalian $p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conditioned on obtaining the outcome $a$, the state of $\\mathsf{Z}$ is then represented by the density matrix $\\sigma_a$ shown in the equation $(2)$, which is obtained by normalizing $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr "Bersyarat pada memperoleh hasil $a$, keadaan $\\mathsf{Z}$ kemudiannya diwakili oleh matriks ketumpatan $\\sigma_a$ yang ditunjukkan dalam persamaan $(2)$, yang diperoleh dengan menormalkan $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generalization {#generalization}"
msgstr "Generalisasi {#generalization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can adapt this description to other situations, such as when the ordering of the systems is reversed or when there are three or more systems.\n"
"Conceptually it is straightforward, although it can become cumbersome to write down the formulas.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh menyesuaikan penerangan ini kepada situasi lain, seperti apabila urutan sistem diterbalikkan atau apabila terdapat tiga sistem atau lebih.\n"
"Secara konseptual ia adalah mudah, walaupun boleh menjadi agak rumit untuk menulis formulanya.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In general, if we have $r$ systems $\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r$, the state of the compound system $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ is $\\rho$, and the measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ is performed on $\\mathsf{X}_k$, the following happens.\n"
msgstr "Secara umum, jika kita mempunyai $r$ sistem $\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r$, keadaan sistem kompaun $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ ialah $\\rho$, dan pengukuran $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ dilakukan pada $\\mathsf{X}_k$, perkara berikut berlaku.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each outcome $a$ appears with probability\n"
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap hasil $a$ muncul dengan kebarangkalian\n"
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Conditioned on obtaining the outcome $a$, the state of $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_{k-1},\\mathsf{X}_{k+1},\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ is then represented by the following density matrix.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}_k}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Bersyarat pada memperoleh hasil $a$, keadaan $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_{k-1},\\mathsf{X}_{k+1},\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ kemudiannya diwakili oleh matriks ketumpatan berikut.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}_k}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}\n"
"$$\n"
